  "family": "vernacular",
  "lineage": "The refined accordion repertoire that grew out of bal-musette from the mid-1930s when Gus Viseur, Tony Murena and Jo Privat absorbed the harmony and swing feel of the Paris manouche jazz scene, giving the fast valse — typically 180-220 beats per minute in 3/4 with the accordion's shimmering wet-tuned tremolo — chromatic passing chords, sixth and ninth voicings, rhythm-guitar la pompe and virtuoso right-hand runs, cut for Odéon and Pathé and later maintained by Yvette Horner and Marcel Azzola.",
